# schoonmakerweb blog safety

## Never repeat this failure mode

1. Live site reads **`src/data/content.json`** (WP catalog).
2. Payload Admin import reads only **`src/content/blog/*.md`**.
3. When `blog/` was empty, CMS looked empty while schoonmakerweb.nl still had articles.
4. New Payload-only posts only go live after sync → **`merge-payload-blog`** → deploy.

## Hard rules

1. Keep **`prepare:blog`**: snapshot → restore-blog-md-from-git → merge-payload → spam hide → validate → floors → assert.
2. Keep **`githubRepo`**: `zbseollp/schoonmakerweb` in `astropayload.config.json` and Tenant Admin.
3. Never delete posts from `content.json` for “spam” — only hide via `spam-slugs.json`.
4. Never soft-warn below `.blog-count-floor` (180) / `.blog-published-floor` (162).
5. Keep canaries in `scripts/blog-canaries.txt` (≥5) and post-build `verify-blog-routes`.
6. After changing `content.json`, run `npm run export:blog-md` and commit the markdown so Payload can re-import.
7. Never add Cloudflare custom-domain `routes` in wrangler.
8. Sort listings by newest of `date` / `modified` (48h future slack stays in `content.ts`).

## If Payload looks empty

1. Filter by tenant **schoonmakerweb**.
2. Force **Import blog** (auto-import skips when any CMS posts already exist).
3. Publish / redeploy so merge brings CMS-only posts into `content.json`.
